1
00:00:12,938 --> 00:00:18,371
Who is on the floor, right now,
and what each of them is doing.

2
00:00:18,823 --> 00:00:23,383
Grouped by workspace, because a person
missing from one site is not missing from

3
00:00:23,383 --> 00:00:23,839
another.

4
00:00:24,290 --> 00:00:30,448
Each one can carry a minimum: the number
of people below which the day does not

5
00:00:30,448 --> 00:00:30,838
work.

6
00:00:31,289 --> 00:00:37,651
Below it, the people asking to be off —
and what each request would cost you.

7
00:00:38,102 --> 00:00:43,025
It says outright when approving one
would drop a day below that floor.

8
00:00:43,476 --> 00:00:48,770
And when the person asking is the only
one who can do a particular job that week.

9
00:00:49,221 --> 00:00:54,654
You decide knowing that, which is the
only version of this decision worth making.

10
00:00:55,107 --> 00:01:00,325
Next: the same thing from the other
side — asking for the day off in the first

11
00:01:00,325 --> 00:01:00,726
place.

